---
// 2026-08-18 visual port. docs/mockups .cred — the strip is now left-aligned h4 + supporting
// line, four up, divided by hairlines, replacing FINAL-v2's centred .credbar.
//
// CONTENT is unchanged and deliberately NOT doc 27 §9.3. §9.3's four cells are Insured /
// Owner-operated / Written scope / region; docs/18-VISUAL-DIRECTION.md §7 (rank 5) mandates
// this bar verbatim as Insured · Organic Pathogen Endorsed · Owner-Operated · region and
// outranks doc 27 (rank 7). That boundary was adjudicated on 2026-08-17 — see
// docs/05-DECISIONS-LOG.md, "CredentialBar.astro flagged mid-session as stale against doc 27
// §9.3 … that was a misread." The port changes the treatment, not the cells.
//
// The one supporting line doc 27 DOES own here — "Founder reviews the scope" (§9.3) — is now
// used verbatim in place of v2's "Founder on every scope", closing the last untraced string
// in this component. Never "licensed" (AGENTS.md §7); no job count, no years figure.
// a11 (2026-08-20) — these four were <h4> and are now <h2>. ELEMENT LEVEL ONLY: the text, the
// order, the `.ac-type-h4` role class, and therefore every computed style are unchanged. The bar
// renders directly under the page <h1> on `/` and on all 14 service pages with no <h2> or <h3>
// between, so h4 skipped two levels on every route it appears on. h2 is the only level that
// skips nothing in that position. Four sibling h2s is correct here — the cells are four peers,
// and adding a wrapper heading to nest them under would be new copy, which this pass is not
// authorized to write.
//
// Why the class stays: type law #1 — size comes from the .ac-type-* role class, never from the
// tag. `.ac-type-h4` wins font-family, size, weight and letter-spacing over the bare `h1,h2,h3`
// element rule on specificity, and both element rules set the same margin and color, so the
// computed styles are byte-identical before and after. Verified, not assumed.
//
// SUPPRESSION, added pre-launch. "Insured" and "Endorsed" were static markup with no data
// connection at all — they rendered unconditionally regardless of `PUBLIC_INSURANCE_STATUS`.
// doc 21 §2.5 requires BOTH the insurance line and the "Organic Pathogen Endorsed" line to be
// matched against a current COI before release; unverified → suppress entirely. No COI is
// verified in this repository today, so both cells are gated on the same env value that
// src/data/site.ts already treats as the insurance-verification signal. The grid renders
// however many cells survive — see the CSS below for why `:first-child` still gets the
// no-left-border treatment regardless of which cells are present.
import { site } from "@data/site";

const insuranceVerified = Boolean(site.business.insuranceStatus);
---

<section class="ac-cred" aria-label="Operating credentials">
  <div class="ac-shell">
    {insuranceVerified && (
      <div>
        <h2 class="ac-type-h4">Insured</h2>
        <p>COI available on request</p>
      </div>
    )}
    {insuranceVerified && (
      <div>
        <h2 class="ac-type-h4">Endorsed</h2>
        <p>Organic pathogen endorsement</p>
      </div>
    )}
    <div>
      <h2 class="ac-type-h4">Owner-operated</h2>
      <p>Founder reviews the scope</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2 class="ac-type-h4">{site.location.regionLabel}</h2>
      <p>Service-area business</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
